# Bug Whisperer — configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in any values you need.
# .env is gitignored (see .gitignore) — never commit it.
#
# This tool runs entirely on your computer. It has no required API keys,
# no cloud services, and no external dependencies for its core features.
#
# The sections below are only needed if you use optional features.

# --- Optional: AI agent integration ---
# The AI-agent skill (SKILL.md) works with any AI coding agent.
# No API keys are needed here — your agent handles its own authentication.

# --- Optional: voice mode ---
# Voice mode requires IBM Watson Speech to Text and Text to Speech.
# If you do not use voice mode, you can ignore these entirely.
# See VOICE.md for setup instructions (if voice mode is enabled).

# IBM Cloud API key (IAM).  Create one at https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/apikeys
# IBM_API_KEY=

# Watson Speech to Text instance URL
# IBM_STT_URL=

# Watson Text to Speech instance URL
# IBM_TTS_URL=

# Watson Text to Speech voice
# IBM_TTS_VOICE=en-US_AllisonV3Voice

# --- Optional: microphone ---
# Voice mode only. Run:  voice.bat --list-mics  to see available devices.
# Leave blank to auto-pick the first audio input device.
# VOICE_MIC=

# Max seconds to record before voice mode stops on its own
# VOICE_MAX_SECONDS=15
